# =============================================================================
# TerraPulse Egypt - report submission endpoint configuration
# =============================================================================
#
# The browser app needs NO environment variables at all. Indicators, charts, the map
# and the choropleth polygons run from embedded datasets, and reports save to
# localStorage; nothing here is read by the SPA.
#
# What lives below is for the one server-side piece: the Cloudflare Pages Function in
# functions/api/reports.js, the only writer to the Neon table. It needs two values.
#
#   NEON_URL  postgresql://web_writer:<password>@<host>/neondb?sslmode=require
#             The migration (db/migrations/0001_neon_physician_reports.sql) creates the
#             table, the row-level-security policy and the INSERT-only `web_writer`
#             role, and deliberately creates the role WITHOUT a password - you set it
#             afterwards, in the Neon SQL Editor (`\password web_writer`) or the
#             dashboard's Roles panel, so no credential transits this file, a commit, or
#             a chat log. Use the pooler endpoint for long-lived TCP connections.
#             Never use neondb_owner: that is owner-level access to every row.
#
#   IP_SALT   Any long random string. It is mixed into the SHA-256 that keys the
#             per-address submission quota, so the stored hash cannot be reversed to an
#             IP and cannot be forged by a caller who does not know the salt. Rotating it
#             resets every address's accumulated window.
#
# Both are SECRET. Neither may ever be named VITE_*: Vite inlines every VITE_ variable
# into the public bundle, so a "VITE_NEON_URL" would publish the credential to anyone
# who can view source - and a connection string, unlike a browser-safe anon key, is
# full access to the database.
#
# Local development: put them in .dev.vars at the project root (gitignored) and run
# `npm run functions`; `npm run dev` proxies /api to that local runtime.
#
# Deployment: `wrangler pages secret put NEON_URL` and `wrangler pages secret put
# IP_SALT` - each reads from stdin, so the value never lands in a shell history file.
#
# Neither value appears in the app's "Report Submission Endpoint" dialog on purpose.
# That dialog shows the endpoint's posture and the migration text, because a physician
# using this build has no business holding a database credential.
